"""
CAN Test Case Generator  -  can_testcase_generator.py
======================================================

Builds a complete CAN communication test specification (Excel) from a Vector
DBC file (native parser, no extra dependency) or an AUTOSAR ARXML file (via the
optional `cantools` package).

For every message the workbook gets one sheet containing
  1. Message definition  - CAN ID to send on, Std/Ext, CAN/CAN FD, BRS, DLC,
     cycle time, send type, transmitters, receivers and ALL message attributes
  2. Bit layout grid      - byte x bit map of every signal (LSB/MSB marked)
  3. Signal definitions   - start bit, length, byte order, value type, initial
     value, factor, offset, min, max, unit, GenSigILSupport, GenSigTimeoutTime,
     GenSigInactiveValue, GenSigStartValue, GenSigSendType, SigType, SPN, value
     table, receivers + every other signal attribute present in the DBC
  4. Test cases           - PASS / CORNER / NEGATIVE / SPECIAL covering value
     range (exact min/max, +/-1 LSB), timing (cycle tolerance, jitter, burst),
     timeout (below/at/above, stop, recovery, start-up), length/DLC, frame format
     (IDE, FDF, BRS, RTR, neighbour IDs), layout (start/end bit, byte order,
     bit isolation, bit shift, unused bits), multiplexing, enum/special values,
     E2E counter/CRC, J1939 special values and signal combinations.
     Every row carries the exact frame to put on the bus (ID, format, DLC,
     payload bytes, Tx mode, cycle, duration) for later CANalyzer/CANoe automation.

Every NEGATIVE row states its Violation Type and Why Negative (the concrete rule
broken, with actual and allowed values); violation counts per type are shown on
Summary and Violation_Summary.

Additional sheets: Summary, Violation_Summary, Message_Index, DBC_Audit,
All_TestCases, Legend.  Full documentation: README.md.
Optional CSV export of all test cases (machine-readable sender contract).

Usage
-----
    GUI       : python can_testcase_generator.py
    CLI       : python can_testcase_generator.py vehicle.dbc -o tests.xlsx --dut BCM
    Nodes     : python can_testcase_generator.py vehicle.dbc --list-nodes
    Self-test : python can_testcase_generator.py --selftest
    Demo      : python can_testcase_generator.py --demo demo_tests.xlsx

Requirements: Python 3.8+, openpyxl.   Optional: cantools (ARXML input).
"""
